{"text": "Dolphins brains have evolved. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Specialized areas dedicated to echolocation. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Allowing them to process acoustic information. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> More quickly and with less energy. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> One key adaptation is the structure of the dolphins auditory pathway. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The signals from the ears. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Are rapidly transmitted to the auditory cortex. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The brain region responsible for processing sound. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> However. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Unlike many other mammals. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Dolphins have a highly specialized auditory cortex. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> With distinct areas. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Dedicated to processing different aspects of echolocation signals. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Some areas may be responsible. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For analyzing the timing of echoes. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> While others focus on the frequency content. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Or the intensity of the sound. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> This specialization allows the dolphins brain. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To process echo information in parallel. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Rather than sequentially. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Imagine a factory assembly line. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Where different workers are responsible. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For different tasks. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> By dividing the work. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Among specialized areas. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The brain can process information. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Much faster and more efficiently. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> This parallel processing reduces. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The cognitive load associated with echolocation. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Allowing dolphins to react quickly. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To changes in their environment.", "alignment": {"characters": ["D", "o", "l", "p", "h", "i", "n", "s", " ", "b", "r", "a", "i", "n", "s", " ", "h", "a", 